{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1510192-influence-water","id":1510192,"title":"Influence Water","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-30T05:06:53-07:00","id":1510192,"title":"Influence Water","content":"I feel like the Ephemeral Influences source book could've done a lot more with the water influence so I came up with a couple additions and changed around a few of the examples. Influence Water is inherently different from Influence Ice and Influence Blood so no Blood or Ice Bending.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Influence Water</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Humidity Control, 1 Dot</b>:<br /> <br /> The entity can increase the humidity around a character, penalizing stamina rolls by the entity's Rank. Rolling an exceptional success inflicts the Fatigue Condition on the character. This doesn't work on Undead obviously.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Surge, 2 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> Calm waters turn into frothing waves, a fire hydrant or water pipe bursts into a deluge. This can cause the Knockdown Tilt to those caught in the onslaught.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Condensation, 3 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> The entity transforms the water vapor in the air into liquid form. The amount of water taken from the air is equal to 1 liter per success and effects an area in yards equal to the entity's Rank. Removing all the moisture from the air transforms it into Dry Air and can have negative impact on the human body represented by the Dehydrated Tilt. (Dehydration Tilt: You suffer a three-die penalty to all rolls, and in scenes of prolonged physical activity, such as combat, you take the severe Sick Tilt on the second round of action. This also doesn't work on Undead obviously.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Rainfall, 3 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> An area the size of a small building or house is afflicted with the Heavy Rains Tilt and, depending on location and Storyteller fiat, can be subjected to the Flood Tilt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Downpour, 4 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> This works like Localized Rainfall, although on a much larger scale. The area targeted is the size of a large neighborhood and is absolutely subjected to the Flood Tilt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Pressurized, 4 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> The entity hits a character with a pressurized jet of water powerful enough to cut through steel. This is treated as a +1 Firearm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>River Dance, 5 Dot:</b><br /> <br /> The entity redirects the flow of a large body of water inland, causing Flooding, Drowning, and massive amounts of property damage.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27672,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","user":"ForsakenProspects","date":". 04-30-2023, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27672-forsakenprospects","name":"ForsakenProspects","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27672_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}